# Ask C.U.R.I.O. — ChatGPT API settings
#
# ─── LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local (git ignores it), paste your key, restart
# `npm run dev`. Without a key the chat still works: it answers straight from
# the local archive, with the same citations.

VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional. Defaults to gpt-4o-mini.
# VITE_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ─── VERCEL / ANY PUBLIC DEPLOY ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Do NOT set VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY in Vercel. Anything named VITE_* is compiled
# into the public JavaScript bundle, so visitors could read the key and spend
# your credits.
#
# Instead, in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, set (no VITE_ prefix):
#
#   OPENAI_API_KEY = sk-...
#   OPENAI_MODEL   = gpt-4o-mini        (optional)
#
# api/curio.js picks those up server-side, and the chat uses it automatically:
# it asks /api/curio on load, and when the function reports a key it stops
# offering the "paste a key" box entirely.
